   "body": "## Words with kanji\n\nKanji often carry a reading above them, called **furigana**: {猫|ねこ} (cat), {お茶|おちゃ} (tea), {日本語|にほんご} (Japanese).\n\n> *{猫|ねこ}が すきです。* — I like cats.\n\n| Kanji | Reading | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| {水|みず} | みず | water |\n| {食|た}べる | たべる | to eat |\n\nKatakana is for loanwords: *タクシー* (taxi), *コーヒー* (coffee).\n\n## Writing kana\n\n```trace\nねがパ\n```\n\nThe words from this lesson are listed below; they join your vocabulary reviews when you complete the lesson."
  }
 ],
